CONFIDENTIAL COMMENTS TO THE EDITOR\par
[(to be withheld from the author(s))].  \par
If necessary, Please include here any comments \par
about why the paper should be accepted or rejected.\par
\par
\par
It is risky for this MM journal to endorse the proposal of
a new database operator that has not been validated by the DB community.
In addition, the symmetric assumption on similarity makes the 
proposed join-operator useless for the CBIR community.  I therefore
cannot recommend this paper to be accepted.
